---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { REPO, STAGES } from "../lib/notes";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="What this site is and how to read it."
  current="about"
>
  <article class="prose max-w-[680px]">
    <h1 class="text-[40px] leading-tight font-semibold">About</h1>
    <p>
      I am Omar Kohl. This site is where I write down notes and thoughts as they
      occur, and revise them when they are no longer correct or up to date.{" "}
      <a href="/writing-more/">Writing More</a> explains why.
    </p>

    <h2>How to read this site</h2>
    <p>
      Notes are not a blog: the order in time matters less than the idea. A note
      is changed in place, and now and then a thread of notes grows into an
      essay. Each page says how settled it is:
    </p>
    <ul>
      {Object.values(STAGES).map((s) => (
        <li>
          {s.symbol} <i>{s.label}</i> — {s.blurb}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p>
      Each note also shows when it was planted, when it was last tended, its
      revision history and the notes that link to it.
    </p>

    <h2>Colophon</h2>
    <p>
      Built with <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a>, set in Source Serif 4
      and searched with <a href="https://pagefind.app/">Pagefind</a>. The source
      is on <a href={REPO}>GitHub</a>. New and revised notes are in the{" "}
      <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
